{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface", "label": "Betaflight SITL Interface - M0 Findings", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_betaflight_sitl", "label": "Betaflight SITL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_betaflight_2026_6_2", "label": "Betaflight 2026.6.2 (pinned tag/commit e0b7bb0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_betaflight_configurator", "label": "Betaflight Configurator (desktop app)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_ofs_sitl_patch", "label": "third_party/betaflight/ofs-sitl.patch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept small and upstreamable on purpose; the osd.c fix is upstream-worthy on its own."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_ofs_sitl_patch_env", "label": "OFS_SITL_PATCH environment variable (none builds stock SITL)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_sitl_udp_ports", "label": "SITL UDP ports (9001 raw PWM, 9002 motors, 9003 state, 9004 RC)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_tcp_uart_ports", "label": "SITL TCP UART ports (5761 MSP, 5762 CRSF, 5763 ESC, 5764 DisplayPort, 5765 SmartAudio)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_legacy_bridge_packet_format", "label": "Legacy bridge fdm_packet format (144 B, ENABLE_GAZEBO_BRIDGE=0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_sign_conventions", "label": "Verified sign conventions (NED/FRD to SITL)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verified 8/8 through motor responses (physics as ground truth, not displays): gyro sent FRD unchanged, accel as (-fx, fy, fz) FRD specific force, quaternion Rx(pi)*q_ned*Rx(pi) with w >= 0. The plan's candidate gyro (x, y, -z) was wrong on yaw. Quaternion/heading mapping remains unverified (compass not fused); Betaflight's internal body frame is FLU. MSP pitch is positive nose-down."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_minimal_arming_config", "label": "Minimal arming config (ARM AUX1, ANGLE AUX2, PWM, small_angle 180)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_sitl_clock_collapse", "label": "SITL clock collapse under request/response pacing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SITL's micros() integrates wall time x simRate, and simRate is re-estimated from packet spacing; under request/response pacing 3.0 s of simulated time left SITL's clock at about 0.66 s, so Betaflight's loop timing, boot grace and RX timeouts ran on a different timebase from the physics."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_lockstep_findings", "label": "Lockstep root causes and patch fixes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stock SITL cannot run in lockstep and GYROPID_SYNC alone does not fix it. The patch pins micros()/millis() to packet timestamps from a fixed 10 s base, runs gyro/filter/PID exactly once per state packet, queues the motor reply in a scheduler-idle hook, merges RC into the state datagram (184 B), and line-buffers stdout - yielding exactly one reply per packet at 6-7x real time with bit-identical runs. Reply ratio 1.0 even with pid_process_denom = 2."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_external_time_flag", "label": "-DENABLE_SIMULATOR_EXTERNAL_TIME=1 (external-time build)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_gyropid_sync", "label": "ENABLE_SIMULATOR_GYROPID_SYNC (insufficient alone for lockstep)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_lockstep_protocol", "label": "Lockstep exchange protocol (184-byte datagram to 9003, 16-byte servo reply from 9002, 1 kHz)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exchange rate must equal Betaflight's virtual gyro rate (one packet = one gyro sample, default 1 kHz); never send to 9004; generous first-reply timeout because TCP 5761 accepting does not mean the main loop runs; one SITL per simulation-time origin since SITL's external clock never runs backwards."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_feature_build_findings", "label": "Feature build results (CRSF RX yes, CRSF telemetry no, ESC partial, DisplayPort yes, SmartAudio partial, Blackbox yes)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_kiss_esc_telemetry", "label": "KISS ESC telemetry frames (battery V/I, RPM, CRC-8 poly 0x07)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "esc_sensor.c sums current and consumption across motors, so the simulator must send per-motor current, not pack current; frames cannot be attributed to motors without DShot telemetry requests, and per-motor RPM never reaches the RPM filter (needs useDshotTelemetry)."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_blackbox_capture", "label": "Blackbox capture (blackbox_device = VIRTUAL writes LOGnnnnn.BFL)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_crsf_telemetry_atomic_shim", "label": "CRSF telemetry needs an ATOMIC_BLOCK shim (not done, M2 work)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_serial_tcp_fixes", "label": "serial_tcp.c UART fixes (rxCallback per byte, baud/mode no-ops)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Interrupt-driven RX drivers never saw TCP bytes: tcpDataIn only filled the buffer, so CRSF and ESC sensor rxCallbacks were never called; serialSetBaudRate/setMode were NULL and crashed SITL when SmartAudio called them."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_osd_c_upstream_bug", "label": "osd.c SIGILL division-by-zero (osdGetBlackboxStatusString / storageTotal, upstream bug)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_wsl2_nat_networking", "label": "WSL2 NAT networking addressing (VM IP + --ip, UDP not forwarded)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TCP localhost forwarding works but UDP does not; send state packets to the WSL VM IP and launch SITL with --ip <host IP as seen from WSL>, binding the motor socket on 0.0.0.0 or the host vEthernet IP. The VM IP changes after wsl --shutdown, so it must be discovered at launch. Mirrored networking would work but changes every distribution, so it stays opt-in."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_stale_sitl_lifecycle", "label": "Stale SITL process lifecycle and cleanup", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Windows does not kill orphaned children: a dead launcher leaves SITL holding UDP 9002-9004; udplink.c uses SO_REUSEADDR so a new SITL binds alongside and only prints 'bind port ... failed', so readiness probes hit the wrong instance. Cleanup before every launch is therefore required: pkill -x betaflight_SITL (never pkill -f, which kills the launching shell). Any 'bind port ... failed' line is a startup error."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_risk_answers", "label": "Answers to spec section 10 risks (M0 evidence)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_m1_plan_assumption_audit", "label": "M1 plan assumption audit (A1-A6 confirmed/refuted)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A3 gyro (x, y, -z) was refuted (real mapping GYRO_SIGN [1,1,1], accel (-fx, fy, fz)); A6 mirrored networking was refuted (NAT + discovered addresses works); the rest confirmed with extensions."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_uart_bytes_in_state_datagram", "label": "UART bytes appended to the lockstep state datagram", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TCP UART bytes arrive on SITL's TCP thread asynchronously to the lockstep tick, so CRSF/ESC/SmartAudio over TCP is not bit-reproducible (M0 section 5 caveat). Carrying UART blocks inside the state datagram, applied on the state thread before the tick, makes receiver traffic deterministic while real tools can still use the TCP UARTs."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_deterministic_boot", "label": "Deterministic boot fix ([SITL] ready for the simulator line)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SITL's UDP thread starts early in systemInit(), so a state packet could land while init still ran and read the fake sensors before or after the packet values; about 40 percent of compared CRSF flights diverged. Fix: ignore state packets until the scheduler runs, announce [SITL] ready for the simulator, run no task before the first packet; the bridge waits for that line instead of probing TCP 5761 and sleeping 300 ms. Result: 8/8 compared flights bit-identical."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_betaflight_reboot_restart", "label": "Betaflight reboot = firmware restart, not a crash", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Configurator Save triggers systemReset() which prints [system]Reset! and calls exit(0); motorShutdown() sleeps about 0.5 s of real time first, longer than the 500 ms reply timeout. The bridge waits up to 3 s for exit 0 plus the reset line, drops the old process, relaunches from the same EEPROM and resends the datagram; State.fc_restarts counts restarts."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_failsafe_timing", "label": "Betaflight failsafe timing (disarm 1.4-2.2 s after link cut, failsafe_delay 1.5 s)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_msp_requires_advancing_time", "label": "MSP serviced only while simulated time advances", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MSP runs inside Betaflight's loop, which only executes while simulated time advances; a paused simulation freezes MSP. This is the reason real-time mode exists and why the harnesses and Configurator need the sim stepping."}, {"id": "docs_research_sitl_interface_patch_generator_tools", "label": "SITL patch generator scripts (add_serial_in_datagram.py, deterministic_boot.py)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_10_04_m0_sitl_spike_t6_windows_py", "label": "t6_windows.py (WSL2 NAT probe from Windows)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_research_sitl_interface", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_04_open_fpv_sim_design", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_sitl_interface_risk_answers", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_10_04_open_fpv_sim_design_spec_10_risks", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_sitl_interface_betaflight_sitl", "target": "docs_research_sitl_interface_betaflight_2026_6_2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_sitl_interface_betaflight_2026_6_2", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_10_04_m0_sitl_spike_build_sitl_sh", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/sitl-interface.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_10_04_m0_sitl_spike_buil